    art: 
    arrival: 'Elsie[sad]: A dark room near the roof, please. I like to be nearer
      the stars.

      And somewhere quiet. Children''s laughter is... difficult.'
    story:
    - 'Elsie[sad]: Arthur went to the front in 1916. I set his place every evening.
      I still do.'
    - 'Elsie: The attic window faces east. Arthur''s letters always came from the
      east.'
    - 'Elsie[happy]: I found his last letter tucked in the lining of my coat. "Don''t
      wait up, love. I''ll find you." So I''ll go and be found.'
    checkout: 'Elsie[happy]: Keep his letter safe for me. I won''t need it where
      I''m going.'
    keepsake: Faded Letter
